   unlockHint:"Synthesized from the five Technical Intelligence Rare cards.",
   fadeDays:120,
   why:"The analytical side of cyber: cryptography, blue team defense, threat intelligence, OSINT, and security architecture. These skills turn technical knowledge into actionable intelligence — the bridge between operator and analyst.",
   howTo:"Work through the intel Rares. Cryptography gives you the theory; blue team gives you detection; threat intel gives you attribution and context; OSINT gives you open-source collection; security architecture gives you design. Together they make you an analyst who can also build.",
   levels:[
     "Explain symmetric vs. asymmetric encryption to a non-technical audience; demonstrate GPG key signing","Configure a SIEM (Splunk, Elastic, or equivalent) with at least 3 data sources and 2 custom detection rules","Produce a threat actor profile for one named APT group using only open sources; cite all sources","Use OSINT to map the network and organizational footprint of a public company (only public sources); written report","Detect and document a simulated adversarial technique (MITRE ATT&CK mapped) in your SIEM","Write a threat intelligence report that includes an executive summary, technical indicators, and recommended detections","Design a zero-trust network architecture for a team of 20; document access controls, segmentation, and monitoring","Attribute a simulated attack to a specific threat actor using forensic + OSINT evidence; brief the finding","Conduct a security architecture review for a real or proposed system; findings adopted by the system owner","Produce a finished intelligence product (OSINT-sourced, threat-intel enriched, architecturally grounded) briefed to a commander","Lead a threat intelligence cell; cell output used to drive real defensive or operational decisions"],
   roadmap:["GPG + crypto explanation","SIEM + detection rules","APT threat actor profile","OSINT network footprint","ATT&CK technique detected","threat intel report","zero-trust architecture design","attack attribution brief","security architecture review","finished intel product briefed","lead threat intel cell"],
