   setKey:"cog2_u_ls_metacognition", synthesizedFrom:"cog2_c_ls_plan_diagnosis", fadeDays:45,
   unlockHint:"This card feeds the Metacognition & Study Strategy Rare.",
   why:"A study plan that isn't working needs a specific diagnosis, not just more hours — the wrong method, the wrong material selection, or poor timing all look the same from the outside but need different fixes. Diagnosing the actual failure is what makes the next session better instead of just longer.",
   howTo:"After an ineffective study session, don't just repeat it — identify specifically why it failed (passive method, wrong material, fatigue, poor spacing) and change that one variable for the next session.",
   levels:["Identify a specific reason one study session was ineffective, not just 'I didn't focus'","Change one specific variable (method, timing, material selection) based on that diagnosis for the next session","Confirm the changed session produced a measurably better outcome (retention, practice score)","Build a real exam prep plan using spaced repetition and active recall as the primary methods, justified by your own diagnosis history","Diagnose and correct an ineffective session in real time, mid-plan, rather than only after the fact"],
   roadmap:["1 session diagnosed","1 variable changed","improvement confirmed","full plan built on diagnosis history","real-time mid-plan correction"],
   advance:["Reach L1: diagnose one bad session specifically","Reach L2: change one variable next time","Reach L3: confirm it worked better","Reach L4: build a full plan from the pattern","Reach L5: correct sessions in real time"],
