   howTo:"In a training scenario, force yourself to name only the ONE most important factor before anything else, then check it against what an after-action review says actually mattered most.",
   levels:["Name the single most important factor in a fast-moving scenario before acting","Confirm your top-priority call against an after-action review in 3+ scenarios","Correctly re-rank priority when a new fact changes what matters most mid-scenario","Distinguish a loud but low-priority cue from a quiet but high-priority one in a live lane","Peak: your first-named priority factor matches the after-action-confirmed priority consistently across varied scenario types"],
   roadmap:["name top factor first","confirm vs AAR x3","re-rank on new info","loud vs quiet cue","peak: consistent match to AAR"],
   advance:["Reach L1: name the single most important factor before acting.","Reach L2: confirm your call against an AAR in 3+ scenarios.","Reach L3: correctly re-rank priority when new information changes the picture mid-scenario.","Reach L4: correctly distinguish a loud low-priority cue from a quiet high-priority one.","Reach L5: peak — first-named priority consistently matches AAR-confirmed priority."],
