   unlockHint:"This card feeds the Body Autonomy & Informed Consent Rare.",
   why:"You can't exercise a right you can't name — knowing exactly what informed consent means and what information you're entitled to is the foundation everything else in this Path builds on.",
   howTo:"Learn and be able to explain, in your own words, what informed consent requires: the diagnosis, proposed treatment, risks, benefits, and alternatives, before you agree to anything.",
   levels:["Write a plain-language definition of informed consent in your own words","List the specific categories of information you're entitled to before a procedure","Explain the difference between consent and mere notification","Identify a real or hypothetical case where consent was skipped or assumed","Correctly explain informed consent to someone else who didn't know the concept"],
